    ],
    "text": "\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      238.75,
      227.27,
      360.18,
      236.13
    ],
    "text": "STATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT",
    "fonts": [
      "TimesNewRoman,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 1,
    "bbox": [
      143.47,
      246.67,
      455.52,
      303.69
    ],
    "text": "Clause 2 : This clause amends section 7 of the Mediation Boards Act, No. 72 of 1988(hereinafter referred to as the \"principal enactment\") and the legal effect of that sectionas amended is to enable the court of First Instance to entertain any application without thecertificate of non settlement, from any party to a dispute in respect of any offencereferred to in second Schedule of the principal enactment, if such party admits such nonsettlement before court or indicate unwillingness to resolve the matter through mediation.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic",
      "TimesNewRoman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      216.21,
      166.97,
      401.69,
      178.31
    ],
    "text": "1Mediation Boards (Amendment)",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      408.81,
      287.83,
      442.54,
      296.9
    ],
    "text": "Short title",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      8.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      202.97,
      235.28,
      214.31
    ],
    "text": "L.D. \u2013 O. 67/2023",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      164.13,
      226.97,
      399.57,
      238.31
    ],
    "text": "AN ACT TO AMEND THE MEDIATION BOARDS ACT, NO. 72 OF 1988",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      250.97,
      401.91,
      274.31
    ],
    "text": "BE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:\u2014",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      286.97,
      401.86,
      310.31
    ],
    "text": "1.This Act may be cited as the Mediation Boards(Amendment) Act, No. of 2024.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      322.97,
      401.89,
      382.31
    ],
    "text": "2.Section 7 of the Mediation Boards Act, No. 72 of1988 (hereinafter referred to as the \"principal enactment\") ishereby amended in paragraph (b) of the proviso to subsection(1) thereof, by the substitution for the words \"that dispute.\"ofthe following:-",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      394.97,
      241.3,
      406.31
    ],
    "text": "\"that dispute:",
    "fonts": [
      "Times"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      185.85,
      418.97,
      401.92,
      526.31
    ],
    "text": "Provided further that, if such certificate of non-settlement is not issued after the expiry of a period ofthree months from the date of making the application,the Court of First Instance shall not be precluded fromentertaining any action in respect of an offence referredto in paragraph (c) of this subsection, if the parties tothe dispute in respect of such offence admit such nonsettlement before court or indicate their unwillingnessto resolve such dispute through mediation.\".",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Italic"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      161.85,
      538.97,
      401.89,
      562.31
    ],
    "text": "3. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times",
      "Times,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 2,
    "bbox": [
      407.85,
      323.59,
      451.29,
      371.06
    ],
